    "sub_name": "批判思考",
    "sub_ename": "CRITICAL THINKING",
    "describe_ch": "Critical thinking is the use of reasoning to determine what is true and what is false. Accordingly, critical thinking is a valuable skill utilised in all disciplines and professions. This Critical Thinking course aims to empower students to think more clearly, insightfully and analytically about what they believe, and be more effective in arguing their views. Students will develop the ability to recognise and avoid common barriers to critical thinking; develop strategies for evaluating evidence and arguments, and learn to formulate and make sound arguments.",
